The known fix — the ORACLE ANSWER for the `tally` playground fixture.

This file is deliberately NOT materialized into the fixture repository (no
MANIFEST line names it), so a coding agent working in a candidate workspace
never sees it. It has two callers, both of them checks:

  * `scripts/materialize-gold-fixture.sh` runs `git apply --check` against every
    freshly materialized tree. That is how the script knows it built the UNFIXED
    fixture, DERIVED from the answer rather than re-spelling the defect in a grep.
  * `--self-test` applies it for real, to prove the suite is RED before and GREEN
    after — the before/after pair that makes the fixture an oracle instead of a
    directory of shell.

Regenerate it (never hand-edit) if `repo/src/tally.sh` changes: materialize the
fixture, edit `tail_last`, and `git -C <dest> diff > test/fixtures/gold-loop/known-fix.patch`.
`git apply` skips this preamble; the diff starts below.

